>> 5) How do you find traps on booby-trapped doors and chests?
>
>Use the #untrap command, of course.
>
The #untrap command seems to work best with the rogue character.  (It's not
unusual for them to start out with an 18 dexterity.)  Once a trap is detected,
there is a chance that one's attempt to #untrap it might actually set it off.
Which I suppose is no worse than if you had never checked.  BTW, like search,
#untrap may take several tries before a trap is detected.

And as others have pointed out, you can only untrap chests (& boxes) and
doors.  IMHO, at the very least, high level rogues should have some chance of
being able to untrap floor traps as well.

>> About genociding gelatinous cubes (very minor possible spoiler).
>> Why would anyone genocide gelatinous cubes? Eating them can give you cold
>> resistance, fire resistance, shock resistance, and possibly more. They
>> are *very* easy to destroy by the time you encounter them.
>
>This was more common in 3.0.  They could paralyze you for quite
>awhile.  Still, they have this annoying tendency to eat anything left
>laying around, especially wood and leather.

About a week ago my character, who had over 100 HP, was weak and decided to
munch on a nearby gelatinous cube.  Well, I hit it once and that was the end
of my character.  First hit paralyzed him, then immediately after he fainted.
Nibbled to death by a gelatinous cube and a small dog.  How humiliating.
